{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/feminisation-of-poverty",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "feminisation of poverty"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "A process in which women and girls are at greater risk of poverty, its deepening, or its persistence due to gender inequalities in access to income, employment, resources, property, and social protection, as well as the unequal burden of unpaid care work."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "It refers not only to the higher proportion of women among people experiencing poverty, but also to the gendered nature of the mechanisms that produce and sustain poverty. In the case of women and girls with disabilities, this risk may be intensified by barriers to education and employment, discrimination, limited access to services and benefits, and additional disability-related costs. The feminisation of poverty can be analysed through income and its sources, employment, economic dependency, care responsibilities, access to benefits and services, housing conditions, and the material consequences of disability."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "3.12.1"
  ],
